    <bpmn:process id="W_W572" name="W572. Customer Credit Monitoring &amp; Automated Alert Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous monitoring via automated credit scoring engine; monthly credit portfolio review meeting
Frequency: Continuous automated monitoring (24/7); monthly portfolio review; quarterly credit policy review
Volume: ~5,200 trade accounts and ~200 corporate accounts monitored continuously; ~50–100 automated alerts per month requiring review
Owner: Credit Manager / AR Supervisor
Participants: Credit Analyst, AR Supervisor, Credit Manager, Finance Manager (I), Sales Manager (C for B2B relationship)
Source: workflow W572 — Customer Credit Monitoring &amp; Automated Alert Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W572_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W572_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W572_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W572_Lane3" name="Credit Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W572_Lane4" name="Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W572_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W572_Start6" name="Continuous monitoring via automated credit scoring engine; monthly credit portfolio…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W572_Task7" name="Credit scoring engine continuously monitors credit portfolio using configured…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Credit scoring engine continuously monitors credit portfolio using configured rules: (a) payment aging trends — rolling 6-month average days-to-pay vs. prior 6-month period; (b) credit utilization % — current outstanding balance / approved credit limit; (c) average days-to-pay trend — acceleration or deceleration; (d) NSF/bounced check history per W1381 — any instance in last 12 months; (e) order-to-invoice ratio — significant drops may indicate customer financial distress (reducing purchases); (f) external signals — credit bureau updates (TransUnion, CIBI) if enrolled
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Continuous (24/7)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W572_Task8" name="Amber alert">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert generation — configurable thresholds trigger tiered alerts: (a) Amber alert (watch list): credit utilization &gt;75%, average days-to-pay increased by &gt;10 days vs. rolling average, first bounced check, order volume drop &gt;30% vs. rolling average; (b) Red alert (action required): credit utilization &gt;90%, any invoice &gt;60 days overdue, second bounced check within 12 months, external credit bureau deterioration, customer under litigation or insolvency filing; alerts queued in Credit Analyst dashboard with priority ranking
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (real-time)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task9" name="Credit Analyst reviews daily alert dashboard: (a) new alerts generated in last…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credit Analyst reviews daily alert dashboard: (a) new alerts generated in last 24 hours; (b) aging of unreviewed alerts (SLA: Amber reviewed within 3 business days, Red reviewed within 1 business day); (c) accounts with multiple concurrent alerts (indicates compounding risk); (d) accounts transitioning from Amber to Red (deterioration trajectory)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task10" name="For Amber alerts: Credit Analyst conducts preliminary review — (a) pull full…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For Amber alerts: Credit Analyst conducts preliminary review — (a) pull full payment history for last 12 months; (b) assess if seasonal pattern (construction industry seasonal slowdown June–September during rainy season) or genuine deterioration; (c) check recent payment notes per W108 collection records; (d) review Sales Manager relationship notes; (e) if seasonal or explainable anomaly → no action, add monitoring note, revisit if trend continues for 2 consecutive months; (f) if unexplained deterioration → upgrade to enhanced monitoring with weekly check-in
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 20–30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task11" name="For Red alerts: Credit Analyst conducts immediate comprehensive review — (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For Red alerts: Credit Analyst conducts immediate comprehensive review — (a) full account history: all invoices, payments, credits, disputes for last 24 months; (b) collection notes per W108 — last contact date, promised payment dates, dispute status; (c) bounced check details per W1381 — amounts, dates, resolution status; (d) order book: open orders and unshipped SOs that would increase exposure; (e) B2B relationship context: discuss with Sales Manager — is customer experiencing project delay, market downturn, or one-time issue?
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 45–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task12" name="Temporary credit hold">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Credit Analyst recommends action based on review: (a) Temporary credit hold — block new sales orders pending payment of overdue amount (system blocks SO creation per W24 authorization matrix); (b) Credit limit reduction — formal notification to customer, reduce limit to current outstanding + 20% buffer; (c) Payment term tightening — change from Net 60 to Net 30, or Net 30 to COD; (d) Cash-on-delivery conversion — remove credit terms entirely, all future transactions COD; (e) No action — false alarm, seasonal pattern, or customer has provided satisfactory explanation with committed payment plan
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 15 min/recommendation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task13" name="Credit Manager approves recommended action: (a) credit hold and credit limit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Credit Manager approves recommended action: (a) credit hold and credit limit changes require Credit Manager approval per W24 authorization matrix; (b) payment term changes require Credit Manager approval with Finance Manager notification; (c) COD conversion requires Credit Manager approval with Sales Manager acknowledgment; (d) Credit Manager reviews recommendation, supporting analysis, and Sales Manager input before decision
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager (for term changes)
Duration: 10–15 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W572_Task14" name="System implements approved credit action: (a) update customer master per W253 —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: System implements approved credit action: (a) update customer master per W253 — credit status, credit limit, payment terms; (b) if credit hold applied: system blocks new sales orders for customer, notifies Sales Manager and assigned Sales Representative, generates hold notification for customer service; (c) generate formal customer notification letter (credit limit change, term change, or COD notification) — reviewed by AR Supervisor for tone and accuracy before sending; (d) all changes logged in credit action audit trail
Responsible (R): System / AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 10 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task15" name="Customer outreach: (a) Sales Manager contacts customer for relationship…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Customer outreach: (a) Sales Manager contacts customer for relationship management — discusses business situation, conveys credit action as temporary measure, explores payment plan or partial payment arrangement; (b) AR Supervisor contacts customer for payment discussion — presents overdue balance details, negotiates payment commitment date, documents agreement in collection notes per W108; (c) if customer provides payment commitment: Credit Analyst monitors follow-through, escalates missed commitment to Credit Manager within 2 business days
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task16" name="Monthly credit portfolio review meeting: Credit Manager, Finance Manager, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly credit portfolio review meeting: Credit Manager, Finance Manager, and Sales Manager review — (a) top 20 exposures by outstanding balance with risk rating; (b) portfolio aging distribution (current, 1–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+ days) vs. prior month; (c) provision adequacy per W81 — compare actual loss experience to provision rates; (d) alert effectiveness metrics — alerts generated vs. actions taken vs. false positives; (e) policy compliance — accounts exceeding credit limit without approval, credit holds overridden; (f) bad debt forecast for next quarter
Responsible (R): Credit Manager / Finance Manager / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task17" name="Quarterly credit policy review: Credit Manager assesses — (a) alert threshold…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Quarterly credit policy review: Credit Manager assesses — (a) alert threshold effectiveness: review Amber-to-Red transition rate, false positive rate, missed deterioration (accounts that defaulted without triggering alert); (b) recommend threshold adjustments to optimize detection vs. false positive balance; (c) update scoring model weights based on latest 12 months of default data; (d) review industry/market risk factors — construction sector outlook, government infrastructure spending, interest rate environment
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W572_Task18" name="Annual credit scoring model calibration: Credit Analyst recalibrates scoring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Annual credit scoring model calibration: Credit Analyst recalibrates scoring model using actual default data — (a) analyze defaulted accounts (written off per W81) vs. performing accounts to identify predictive factors; (b) update weighting of risk factors (utilization, aging, bounced checks, external scores); (c) back-test revised model against historical data; (d) present calibration results to Finance Manager for approval; (e) deploy updated model parameters to production
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1 week/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W572_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W572_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W572_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W572_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-286 (ensure controlled execution — Credit Application &amp; Scoring (PA-16.1).) | - operational: conservative initial credit limits per W24 and proactive monitoring; operational: relying primarily on internal payment behavior data; operational: Sales Manager relationship context (step 9) before taking credit action
Owner: Credit Manager / AR Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
