    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1300" name="W1300. Trade Account Credit Limit Annual Review, Adjustment &amp; Exposure Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual credit review cycle (each account reviewed on the anniversary of credit approval); or triggered by payment pattern deterioration (30+ days past due); or customer request for credit limit increase
Frequency: ~5,200 annual reviews (one per active trade account per year); ~500–800 ad-hoc reviews triggered by payment deterioration
Volume: ~5,200 active trade AR accounts representing 30% of revenue (~PHP 18.7B/year)
Owner: Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Participants: Credit &amp; Collections Manager, Credit Analyst, Sales Manager (Trade), CFO, Customer
Source: workflow W1300 — Trade Account Credit Limit Annual Review, Adjustment &amp; Exposure Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1300_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1300_Lane1" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1300_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1300_Lane3" name="Credit &amp; Collections Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1300_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1300_Start5" name="Annual credit review cycle (each account reviewed on the anniversary of credit approval)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1300_Task6" name="Annual review scheduling &amp; data compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual review scheduling &amp; data compilation: (a) system generates monthly batch of accounts due for annual review (by credit approval anniversary month); (b) Credit Analyst compiles review package per account: (i) payment history over past 12 months (on-time %, average days past due, highest aging bucket reached), (ii) purchase volume trend (increasing, stable, declining), (iii) current outstanding balance vs. credit limit utilization, (iv) number of credit limit increase requests in past 12 months, (v) any returned checks or payment disputes, (vi) external credit bureau data (if available — Philippine credit bureaus like CIC, TransUnion Philippines)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1300_Task7" name="Credit scoring recalculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Credit scoring recalculation: System recalculates credit score using updated data: (a) payment score (40% weight): on-time payment rate, average days past due, returned check count; (b) volume score (20% weight): purchase volume trend and consistency; (c) utilization score (20% weight): credit limit utilization rate — chronically maxed-out accounts score lower; (d) tenure score (10% weight): years as BuildRight trade customer; (e) external score (10% weight): credit bureau score if available; (f) resulting score maps to credit tier: (i) Platinum (score ≥ 85): credit limit up to PHP 5M, terms Net 60, (ii) Gold (score 70–84): credit limit up to PHP 2M, terms Net 30, (iii) Silver (score 55–69): credit limit up to PHP 500K, terms Net 30, (iv) Bronze (score 40–54): credit limit up to PHP 200K, terms Net 30 with 10% holdback, (v) Probation (score &lt; 40): credit limit reduced to PHP 50K or suspended, COD terms
Responsible (R): System / Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: Automated scoring + 5 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1300_Task8" name="Credit limit decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credit limit decision: Credit Analyst reviews score and recommends: (a) maintain current limit and terms, (b) increase limit and/or improve terms (for improving accounts), (c) decrease limit and/or tighten terms (for deteriorating accounts), (d) suspend credit and convert to COD (for severely deteriorating accounts); for limit increases &gt; PHP 1M: Credit &amp; Collections Manager approval required; for limit increases &gt; PHP 3M: CFO approval required; for credit suspension: Credit &amp; Collections Manager approval with Sales Manager notification
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager (or CFO for large increases)
Duration: 5–10 min per account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1300_Task9" name="Customer communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer communication: (a) for credit limit increases: system sends notification to customer with new limit and terms — positive engagement opportunity; (b) for credit limit decreases: Credit Analyst calls customer to explain change, discusses remediation path (e.g., &quot;bring all payments current within 60 days and your score will improve&quot;); (c) for credit suspension: Sales Manager and Credit Analyst meet with customer to discuss: is the account salvageable? can customer provide additional guarantees (personal guarantee of company owner, post-dated checks)?; (d) all decisions documented in ERP credit management module
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 10–20 min per account (for decreases/suspensions)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1300_Task10" name="Portfolio-level exposure monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Portfolio-level exposure monitoring: Monthly, Credit &amp; Collections Manager reviews portfolio-level exposure: (a) total AR outstanding vs. portfolio credit limit (total approved limits), (b) aging distribution: current, 1–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+ days, (c) concentration risk: top 20 accounts as % of total AR, (d) industry segment exposure (construction, government projects, interior design, etc.), (e) bad debt provision adequacy: actual write-off rate vs. provision rate, (f) report to CFO with recommendations for portfolio-level action (tighten new credit approvals, increase bad debt provision, engage collection agency for 90+ accounts)
Responsible (R): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1300_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1300_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1300_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1300_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-286 (ensure controlled execution — Credit Application &amp; Scoring (PA-16.1).) | - operational: Credit &amp; Collections Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Credit &amp; Collections Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1300_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1300_Annotation12" targetRef="W1300_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow14" sourceRef="W1300_Start5" targetRef="W1300_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow15" sourceRef="W1300_Task6" targetRef="W1300_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow16" sourceRef="W1300_Task7" targetRef="W1300_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow17" sourceRef="W1300_Task8" targetRef="W1300_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow18" sourceRef="W1300_Task9" targetRef="W1300_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1300_Flow19" sourceRef="W1300_Task10" targetRef="W1300_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
